{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"GUARD-INTENT RESOLUTION (sharpens remediation ranking): the pack-size limit was introduced by commit 16a1a385 (ticket 037b-879e-fe13-47d2, 2026-08-01) whose message is explicit: 'Add blobless fetches and executable pack-size BUDGETS. Guard authorship verification with exact object-database snapshots so identity scans cannot lazily fetch promisor objects.' => The 100 MiB limit is a DELIBERATE budget on the tickets-history blobless checkout (a growth canary), NOT an accidental inclusion of the tickets branch. The workflow also GENUINELY needs full tickets history (the 'Mount tickets branch' step fetches it un-shallow for commit-ancestry-scoped signature verification). CONSEQUENCE: remediation option (1) 'scope verify-identity's checkout to drop tickets' is INVALID — it would silence an intentional budget/canary while the store is genuinely over budget (independently confirmed by the data-disk-high alarm 5a05). Valid levers are only: raise the budget (stopgap leash), bound growth (4520 apparent-sighted-cockatoo), and reclaim existing mass (536b polite-antivirus-bedbug causal-stability GC — the ONLY lever that returns the pack under budget without raising it)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788027697136855001,"uuid":"1de6d6d6-ff47-400a-b881-ee13111572a1"}